From 8a17c234c4ed6f41a09c04fe916569fda3f52b37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:28:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] egl/wayland: free the spare buffers of idle window
 surfaces

Spare colour buffers are only trimmed in update_buffers(), which runs
when the client draws again. A surface that stops drawing, such as a
wallpaper or an idle panel, keeps every buffer it ever needed for triple
buffering for as long as it lives: one or two full-size buffers that the
compositor has already released.

Add one thread per display that waits until a window surface has not
swapped for 3 seconds, takes in the releases already queued for it and
frees every colour buffer that is not locked, not on screen and not the
back buffer. If the compositor still holds a spare at that point, the
thread looks again after 1, 2 and 4 seconds and then leaves the surface
alone until its next swap, so an idle surface costs at most four
wakeups. The next swap allocates a back buffer as it does after a
resize, and query_buffer_age reports 0 for it, so clients repaint fully.

The thread only sees releases that have already been read from the
display socket, so a client that never reads its display keeps its
buffers as before.

Every path that touches color_buffers or dispatches the surface queue
(image_get_buffers, swap after the glthread flush, query_buffer_age) now
holds a per-surface lock. The thread only try-locks it and never waits
on a surface that is drawing. The thread takes trim_mtx and then
try-locks trim_lock, while the swap path takes trim_lock and then
trim_mtx; because the thread never blocks on trim_lock while it holds
trim_mtx, the two orders cannot deadlock.

The wait uses a monotonic condition variable, so a change of the wall
clock neither stretches nor skips it.

At 3024x1964 (an M4 MacBook Pro panel) each such buffer is 23 MiB.

A surface leaves the trim list before its DRI drawable is destroyed, so
the thread never walks a surface that is being torn down.

(cherry picked from commit 4069c313b36430289a6b4aa8bcd48fabb08865c5)
